ttp';\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-root',\n  templateUrl: './app.component.html',\n  styleUrls: ['./app.component.css']\n})\nexport class AppComponent {\n  constructor(private http: HttpClient) {}\n\n  getData() {\n    this.http.get('https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts').subscribe((data: any[]) => {\n      console.log(data);\n    });\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis code sends an HTTP GET request to a JSONPlaceholder API and logs the response data to the console. You can replace 'https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts' with your own API endpoint. Make sure to use HTTPS for secure communication, and always validate user input before sending requests to prevent security vulnerabilities.\n```\n```"
